  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're verified, Yusuf. Thanks.\n\n**Order #6601 (Spice Route):** I looked into the wrong item. Spice Route has an open incident right now. Their supplier recalled a batch of sauce used in their curries, and it affects orders placed between 5:00 and 7:00 pm today. You placed yours at 6:58 pm, so it falls inside that window.\n\nThat means I can't refund or credit this order myself. Forkful's incident team handles compensation for every affected order. I've sent them your case with the details: you ordered paneer makhani ($15.00) and got chicken makhani. The reference is **ESC-700**, and a specialist will contact you within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll offer, but they have everything they need.\n\n**Please don't eat the chicken makhani or any other curry from this order.** The recall covers the sauce. I'm glad nobody has eaten it yet. If anyone does eat it and feels unwell, tell me right away so I can flag it as a food-safety issue too.\n\nWhat went wrong with your other orders? I see #6602 from Spice Route and #6603 from Lotus Garden tonight."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, a recall? Nobody's eaten any of it, so that's good, but that's a bit alarming. And the incident team will reach out in 24 hours? My guests are arriving soon, so that's not going to help me tonight.\n\nOkay, #6602 is the second Spice Route order I placed a few minutes after the first one. I ordered extra garlic naan and only one of the two naans came. Can I get that refund to my card?"
