  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've refunded **$7.00** to your Visa ending 4242 for the missing spring rolls. It should arrive within 3\u20135 business days.\n\n**About #6601:** yes, it's really happening. Your case is filed with the incident team under reference **ESC-700**, and a specialist will contact you within 24 hours. They'll have the details: you ordered paneer makhani ($15.00), got chicken makhani, and nobody ate it. You don't need to do anything else. If you hear nothing within 24 hours, contact us and give that reference number.\n\n**Here's where everything stands tonight:**\n- **#6601 (Spice Route):** sent to the incident team (ESC-700). Please don't eat the curry from this order.\n- **#6602 (Spice Route):** $4.00 refunded for the missing garlic naan.\n- **#6603 (Lotus Garden):** $7.00 refunded for the missing spring rolls.\n\nYou'll also see a pending hold for each order on your card statement. Those aren't extra charges. They're temporary holds from when you ordered, and they'll drop off within 1\u20133 business days.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with? I hope the evening with your friends goes well."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for sorting the naan and spring rolls. The $4 and $7 refunds are what I wanted.\n\nStill not thrilled about #6601 being left to the incident team with no real answer until tomorrow, but I have the reference number ESC-700 if they don't reach out. I'll keep an eye out for it.\n\nI'll go check on my guests now. Thanks."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Yusuf. I understand the wait on #6601 is frustrating, and I'm sorry I couldn't settle it tonight. Keep ESC-700 handy in case you don't hear back within 24 hours.\n\nOne last reminder: please set aside the chicken makhani from #6601 so nobody eats it by mistake. If anyone does eat it and feels unwell, contact us right away.\n\nEnjoy the rest of your evening with your friends!"
  }
